  "theorem": "For a finite stochastic coarse-graining C, a deep linear effect is exactly visible at the coarse layer iff it lies in range(C^T). Two deep states are operationally indistinguishable at that layer iff their difference lies in ker(C). For a hierarchy C_n...C_1, visible-effect spaces are nested and their dimensions equal the ranks of the successive composites. An exact linear decoder on all states exists iff C has full column rank; a stochastic decoder additionally requires positivity."
